  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nIn a discussion around wake lock, folks realized that there are potentially several use cases for an API which would require transient activation for initial usage, but might not want to require transient activation for subsequent usage. The specific use case discussed was a page which acquired wake lock, then went into the background and lost wake lock, but then desired to reacquire wake lock when it became visible again.\n\nIf there are indeed additional use cases, it might make sense to define a concept in HTML that would make this kind of requirement clear. I have no idea what to call it, but clever people like @marcoscaceres and @reillyeon might (and might also be able to describe the use cases they're considering).\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n_No response_\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
